{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>When the gates of Jerusalem cast shadows</b> — from the root of צל (shadow); the sense is the arrival of the shadow upon the gates." "<b>No burden shall enter</b> — he explained: that the peddlers, who are the merchants, should not enter; ערבים has many meanings, therefore from the idea of mixing things together רכיל (talebearer) is so called."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The argument turns on the root ערב in its various senses; rendered hyper-literally without expanding the compressed wordplay."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:42.896044291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}